      "message": "We can avoid having to copy the de-duplicated color data if we move the logic down to after we allocate `fStorage` and assign `fColors`. \n\nIt\u0027s a relatively rare case to need to prune duplicate colors (and when they are pruned, it probably won\u0027t be that many to remove), so it\u0027s not unreasonable to allocate with the original `fColorCount` and then reduce it as we encounter duplicate stops.\n\nAlternatively, we can do an iteration here to count the number of duplicates that would get removed in order to keep the count exact.",
