      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thinking about terminology, `leftmost` and `rightmost` are bit easier to interpret from the inner/outer that we\u0027d been using initially. Assigning to `bools` with descriptive names can also help here, something like:\n\n    // Include the leftmost (i) when not a duplicate, or not already on the left\n    // edge (t \u003d 0), or we are on the left edge but are clamping to it.\n    const bool includeLeftmost \u003d !dupStop || desc.fPositions[i] !\u003d 0 || fTileMode \u003d\u003d SkTileMode::kClamp;\n    // Include the rightmost (j-1) when it is a duplicate range and we aren\u0027t\n    // already on the right edge (t \u003d 1), or we are on the right edge but are\n    // clamping to it\n    const bool includeRightmost \u003d dupStop \u0026\u0026 (desc.fPosition[j-1] !\u003d 1 || fTileMode \u003d\u003d SkTileMode::kClamp);\n    \n    \nI also think in the check for desc.fPosition \u003d\u003d 1 (or !\u003d1), we should be checking `j-1` to see if the RHS of the duplicate interval is at t\u003d1.",
